{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge","id":1077119,"title":"A Walk in the Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T12:18:34-07:00","id":1077119,"title":"A Walk in the Hedge","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/1077055-a-walk-in-the-hedge-changeling-the-lost\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/1077055-a-walk-in-the-hedge-changeling-the-lost\"> A walk in the Hedge [Changeling: The Lost] - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/1077055-a-walk-in-the-hedge-changeling-the-lost\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/1077055-a-walk-in-the-hedge-changeling-the-lost </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hi, folks, Rose here. ^_^ Today, I&rsquo;d like to share more about the fundamentals of the*Changeling setting through an excerpt from Chapter 2, covering the Hedge and the beings who live there. Without further ado&hellip;. The Hedge The Hedge is always around the edges of the mundane world. In the lonely places, where yours is the only breath stirring the air; in the uncanny places, where fear quickens your step; in the liminal places, where you hang in the balance between here and there. An abandoned office park, weedy grass breaking through broken asphalt; a graveyard, Spanish moss hanging from </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:32:26-07:00","id":1077131,"title":"","content":"The Hedge is such a cool place, why do I have to live on Earth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . All this does is make me screech for Changeling 2E release even more. PLEASE RELEASE IT GOD I'M SO EXCITED <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />!!!!<br /> <br /> I love some of the concepts for Changeling 2E like the Huntsman , God It's going to be so good ^-^ !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:55:45-07:00","id":1077144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077131#post1077131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge is such a cool place, why do I have to live on Earth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can go live there if you like!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:21:46-07:00","id":1077163,"title":"","content":"I'm... Honestly not sure what I was meant to take away from that. It felt too prosaic; too scattered. I don't have any idea what the Hedge looks like apart from a bit of a psychedelic experience, nor any sense of what it is, why I'd go there... There was more word count spent on the florid examples than on describing what the Hedge actually is.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I didn't like the Hedge being taken in the &quot;PAIN PAIN PAIN ONLY PAIN MY GOODNESS WHY DID YOU EVEN COME HERE PAIN PAIN PAIN&quot; direction, so I'm refreshed to see that something different is taking shape, but I haven't really got any clue from that what that shape actually is.<br /> <br /> What is the Hedge meant to be? What does it look like? What role is it fulfilling? Do I not have to relive my abusive father treating me to the Orwell Special to get some magic fruit anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:36:21-07:00","id":1077179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077163#post1077163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Hedge meant to be? What does it look like? What role is it fulfilling? Do I not have to relive my abusive father treating me to the Orwell Special to get some magic fruit anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the assessment that it's exceptionally vague in where the Hedge stands now. I assume we still get hollows and all the fruit and 1ed goodness. Do we still get Dreams connected to the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:22:28-07:00","id":1077214,"title":"","content":"Hi all! I'm Meghan, Rose's co-developer on this book. I figured I'd pop in and say hello.<br /> <br /> Dreams are indeed connected to the Hedge! The systems chapter delves into how to use and traverse the Hedge as a player character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:25:28-07:00","id":1077221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077144#post1077144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you can go live there if you like!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can?!?!!?! Oh boy - I'm going to have all the goblins fruits ^-^. <br /> <br /> Overall, I like the switch in writing between &quot;Once&quot; and &quot;Now&quot;...Now it has me wondering what caused it to change. I know the Hedge is ever-changing but it sounds like a big change happened. Hmm.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I also feel it keeps true to much of 1E Changeling's feel. God I want the book now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Excellent work Changeling Dev Team!<br /> <br /> Also if I may - why is was Dreaming Roads redacted from the preview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:27:52-07:00","id":1077223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077214#post1077214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all! I'm Meghan, Rose's co-developer on this book. I figured I'd pop in and say hello.<br /> <br /> Dreams are indeed connected to the Hedge! The systems chapter delves into how to use and traverse the Hedge as a player character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello Meghan - Keep up the excellent work; hyped for the book ^.^<br /> <br /> Question: Will the book go into how other splats interact with the Hedge in more detail? Specifically for Cross-Over Games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:28:13-07:00","id":1077225,"title":"","content":"It should be remembered this is an <i>excerpt </i>from chapter 2. More concrete details about the Hedge, which include the rules for navigating it and interacting with the thorns, are probably elsewhere, as was in fact previewed before.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sniped by a developer!<br /> <br /> I like the poetic tone and the interesting bits and pieces of people finding the Hedge and individuals' relationships with goblins after being taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-12-2017, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:43:30-07:00","id":1077236,"title":"","content":"The Hedge definitely isn't pain and bad memories all the time! Sometimes, the Hedge does reflect what you bring in, but it's not the inside of your own head -- it's a place of its own, with its own geography and inhabitants.<br /> <br /> As for what the Hedge literally is, from the introduction:<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt;<br /> Arcadia is separated from the human world by the Hedge. More than just a borderland, the Hedge is a world in its own right, full of people and places and strange sights. The Hedge often takes cues from the places where it touches the Ironsides or Arcadia, but develops them in its own way. For example, the late Widow Gulch's abandoned house at the end of your block might be echoed by a wooden frame and tattered insulation in the Hedge... but rather than a suburban neighborhood, it might be on an island in a flooded wonderland or used as billboard space in a goblin market the size of Manhattan. Changelings move frequently between the Hedge and the human world, but many hobgoblins live their entire lives in the Hedge's thickets and caves and odd little villages.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is replete with secret passages and hidden niches, and since not even the True Fae know them all, changelings can carve out Hollows here and bargain with Hedge residents for advantages. The Hedge also affords Courts and characters the opportunity to claim fae territory as well as mundane territory.<br /> <br /> The Hedge's tendency to change on its own can make it seem dreamlike and unreal... but changelings know that that it's as true and dangerous as anything else they experience.<br /> <br /> Look to the Hedge for opportunities to make the journey as colorful as the destination, and as a source of obstacles and creative solutions to problems you didn't even know you had.<br /> &gt;&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:56:12-07:00","id":1077242,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey, Ironside(s) is getting canonized? That's cool. I'm bummed to see the Hedge lose the pain angle David was taking it in, as that has spoken strongly to me. This direction is interesting though.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, the more I'm seeing of new Changeling, the more I'm glad David posted as much of his version as he did. This is looking more and more like it's going to be a completely different game than the one we've seen previewed, and it's still too soon to know if I will like this one as much as I did that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:10:26-07:00","id":1077256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077214#post1077214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all! I'm Meghan, Rose's co-developer on this book. I figured I'd pop in and say hello.<br /> <br /> Dreams are indeed connected to the Hedge! The systems chapter delves into how to use and traverse the Hedge as a player character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes me so happy to hear! I loved the playtest of Dreams and it made so much sense for glamour from mortal dreams to trickle into the hedge and feed it, and for hobs and critters to be born out of those dreams. I've been very anxious that all my favorite parts would just be scrapped. I'm sure what you're doing is going to be good, but it's a question of Awesome Thing In Hand versus the Unknown Element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:42:54-07:00","id":1077292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077221#post1077221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if I may - why is was Dreaming Roads redacted from the preview?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're probably going to talk about them more in the future. But, so as not to be cryptic: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hidden trails lead from the Hedge into human dreams. They are quiet and furtive paths that wend their way around wonders and perils, leading into the Hedge just as the Hedge fades into Faerie. These are the Dreaming Roads, and the Gentry know them well\u2026 but so do their erstwhile captives. Through the little piece of Faerie within herself, one of the Lost can find upon the Dreaming Roads and walk among sleepers. By finding the entrance within herself, the oneiropomp \u2014 the wanderer of dreams \u2014 can follow the path into almost any dream. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:57:15-07:00","id":1077304,"title":"","content":"Speaking of dreams, are changelings still going to vanish when they sleep by default? That was one of the few things that I hadn't cared for in the previews. It seemed odd to me that choosing one of the two dreaming gates would result in no dreams at all. Granted, it is a simple house rule to say that one gate causes them to vanish into lucid dreams, one gives them normal dreams but removes their special defenses against other dream manipulators, or they can choose neither of them, resulting in no dreams at the cost of their Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:00:15-07:00","id":1077306,"title":"","content":"No, changelings don't vanish when they fall asleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:08:37-07:00","id":1077315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077306#post1077306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, changelings don't vanish when they fall asleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! Thanks for letting me know. I can't wait to get my hands on this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:22:30-07:00","id":1077321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077304#post1077304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seemed odd to me that choosing one of the two dreaming gates would result in no dreams at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was because changelings were physical in dreams, so if you choose to dream... then you'll physically be in the dream. If you want to stay where you are, then you choose to not go into the dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:04:39-07:00","id":1077340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077321#post1077321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was because changelings were physical in dreams, so if you choose to dream... then you'll physically be in the dream. If you want to stay where you are, then you choose to not go into the dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I thought that was really cool. I do hope they still physically enter dreams, even if their own dreams don't work that way any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:21:01-07:00","id":1077347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077340#post1077340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I thought that was really cool. I do hope they still physically enter dreams, even if their own dreams don't work that way any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entering a dream is literally walking a path. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (You may notice that one of my big pushes on <i>Changeling</i> is that everything is very real and true and often physical. Changelings have been constantly told that their perceptions are wrong, constantly had their sense of selves and belief in their own lucidity eroded by sources both faerie and mortal. And people like the Gentry think that they can get away with that, because they can make reality unreliable. But they can't. Changelings have a right to their experiences, and neither the subjectivity of human perspective nor the malleability of the Hedge nor the Others' world-changing powers can take that away.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:54:08-07:00","id":1077366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077321#post1077321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was because changelings were physical in dreams, so if you choose to dream... then you'll physically be in the dream. If you want to stay where you are, then you choose to not go into the dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I understood that part. The part that bothered me was using the gates of horn and ivory for it. The original story of them had one gate take you to true dreams and one take you to false ones. The game version had one gate taking you to true dreams and the other to no dreams at all. That's why I was going to house rule that taking either gate would lead to dreams, and give changelings the option to choose &quot;none of the above&quot;. I'm definitely curious about how they dream in the new edition, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:22:44-07:00","id":1077385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077163#post1077163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Hedge meant to be? What does it look like? What role is it fulfilling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this sentiment here. The writeups here are beautiful, but of little use for conceptualizing the Hedge itself. Is the former writeup on how the Hedge focuses on stings, shocks and aches still valid? Or are we swapping that out for something more like a living daydream?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:12:20-07:00","id":1077418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077347#post1077347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entering a dream is literally walking a path. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (You may notice that one of my big pushes on <i>Changeling</i> is that everything is very real and true and often physical. Changelings have been constantly told that their perceptions are wrong, constantly had their sense of selves and belief in their own lucidity eroded by sources both faerie and mortal. And people like the Gentry think that they can get away with that, because they can make reality unreliable. But they can't. Changelings have a right to their experiences, and neither the subjectivity of human perspective nor the malleability of the Hedge nor the Others' world-changing powers can take that away.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very reassuring to hear. Above all I loved how David's version of Changeling dealt with the game's themes of abuse and trauma in a very direct and honest way. Knowing that that, at least, isn't going away helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:19:07-07:00","id":1077425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077418#post1077418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very reassuring to hear. Above all I loved how David's version of Changeling dealt with the game's themes of abuse and trauma in a very direct and honest way. Knowing that that, at least, isn't going away helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's put it this way: I'm a survivor, and the first header in the Writer's Guide is &quot;Survivor Stories.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:29:12-07:00","id":1077431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077214#post1077214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all! I'm Meghan, Rose's co-developer on this book. I figured I'd pop in and say hello.<br /> <br /> Dreams are indeed connected to the Hedge! The systems chapter delves into how to use and traverse the Hedge as a player character.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pleasure to meet you (do forums count as meeting someone, maybe communicating would be a better term).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:46:37-07:00","id":1077445,"title":"","content":"There are some cools parts like how technology works in the hedge, but other parts are just confusing, like I had to read it twice to figure out what you we're talking about. <br /> <br /> Like the first Once was referring to a examples of humans being taken by their keeper and giving examples, but honestly it wasn't clear as typing Once really doesn't transition well, it offer no context like I didn't realize what the Statue person was a True Far until the Statue Grab the human to kidnap them. maybe maybe &quot;Once You Were Lured and Taken&quot;, instead of just using &quot;Once&quot; as a header would give a reader a better heads up as to what going on in the part. <br /> <br /> Just a better transition as to what your referring too. <br /> <br /> And the Thorns need some love, they're a key part of the Hedge, but they aren't mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:53:10-07:00","id":1077663,"title":"","content":"Am I getting it right that now in Hedge we can have GHOSTS? Like 'unresolved dead ones leftovers' ghosts in from rest of CoD universe? If yes, I'm more than happy for that. I always wanted to add 'dead ones' to my fairy tale stories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:02:59-07:00","id":1077672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077663#post1077663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I getting it right that now in Hedge we can have GHOSTS? Like 'unresolved dead ones leftovers' ghosts in from rest of CoD universe? If yes, I'm more than happy for that. I always wanted to add 'dead ones' to my fairy tale stories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the Gravewrights need something to do...<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, it's been mentioned that changelings and ghosts have a lot of things in common, so many goblins being the unquiet only fits.<br /> <br /> I'm more interested by the implication you can have a ghost of someone who is technically, y'know...alive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T09:38:28-07:00","id":1077771,"title":"","content":"It also suggests the possiblity that the Hedge now has a twilight stage, just as Ironside does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T09:40:16-07:00","id":1077772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077663#post1077663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I getting it right that now in Hedge we can have GHOSTS? Like 'unresolved dead ones leftovers' ghosts in from rest of CoD universe? If yes, I'm more than happy for that. I always wanted to add 'dead ones' to my fairy tale stories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They're part of our initiative to flesh out Hedge denizens more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here's a bit from Chapter 5:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 5</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to get lost in the Hedge. It's easy to wander among the brambles, hoping for a break in the growth and a glimpse of familiar ground that never comes. It's easy to stumble into a pit lined with walls that weep real tears, sadness slicking the surface so you can't climb back out. It's easy to crash through the branches into an open area, only to find you've wandered into a circle of hungry trolls arguing over which protein goes best with their stew. (Surprise, it's you.)<br /> <br /> It's easy to <i>die</i> in the Hedge, and the dead tend to stick around.<br /> <br /> Not all Hedge ghosts, however, are former changelings or humans. Emotions shape the Hedge: strong impressions of fear and pain, joy and rapture, feelings that can grow so overwhelming that they awaken as their own entities. Travelers passing through the Hedge also leave pieces of themselves behind, bits of their souls that snag on the Thorns. A potent enough Icon may detach itself and continue wandering, or be gathered up by a hobgoblin seamstress and sewn into something new, made entirely out of other scraps of souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:03:45-07:00","id":1077782,"title":"","content":"Love that imagery, I can see myself making use of the hedge when ever i can get my mits on the new edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:49:24-07:00","id":1077795,"title":"","content":"&quot;Not all Hedge ghosts, however, are former changelings or humans. Emotions shape the Hedge: strong impressions of fear and pain, joy and rapture, feelings that can grow so overwhelming that they awaken as their own entities. Travelers passing through the Hedge also leave pieces of themselves behind, bits of their souls that snag on the Thorns. A potent enough Icon may detach itself and continue wandering, or be gathered up by a hobgoblin seamstress and sewn into something new, made entirely out of other scraps of souls&quot;<br /> <br /> That is really freaking cool, I like that. It makes me think of Chthorathions (I never remember how to spell those right), but with a more Fae flavour. <br /> <br /> They use the mechanics of ghosts, like <br /> Cthorathions, but also like Cthorathions the Never Born, they aren't really ghosts.<br /> <br /> I'm calling them Icon Ghosts and Glamour Ghosts for now.<br /> <br /> Anyways would a Mage manipulate these ghosts using fate or death arcana or a mix? What about a <br /> Goblin's Ghost?<br /> <br /> I could see a Court Contract for summoning/creating/commanding the Glamour (emotional) Ghosts related to the Court's emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:55:30-07:00","id":1077800,"title":"","content":"I had an idea where you could still use the Hedge is pain idea in this new Hedge as parts of the Hedge near Ironside locations were alot of pain occurred, sites of mass murders, mass torture sites, common places to commit suicides, accident prone work sites, hospitals, homeless shelters, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:57:50-07:00","id":1077802,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the Hedge is back to &quot;generally psychoreactive&quot;. That's nice<br /> <br /> Also, glad we have Hedge Ghosts. Various supernatural researchers trying to figure out their relationship to real ghosts has a lot of story seed potential. Not to mention how interchangeable fae and spirits of the dead have been in folklore for centuries","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T11:45:39-07:00","id":1077826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077236#post1077236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look to the Hedge for opportunities to make the journey as colorful as the destination, and as a source of obstacles and creative solutions to problems you didn't even know you had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much more what I was after. I mean that to all you said, but this is what I was hoping the Hedge would be. Personally, I'm <i>very</i> curious how you'll manage it.<br /> <br /> The goblins bit is great, too, as is the presence of ghosts; not just of people, but of memories, ideas, ideals, hopes, and dreams. I like that the Hedge can be a place where a Changeling can meet a zeitgeist and explore the emotional power and resonance of such things. It's delightful to think one meet the incarnate form of a nostalgia for a time or place they never lived in, or beings that encompass all the powerful feelings and emotions of the human soul.<br /> <br /> I like this direction. I like that subtext is not being made into text here. I like that the setting can carry resonances without needing to tell you up-front what it's a metaphor for, and be open enough that you can use it either for its surface value or for deeper feelings as befits the game.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the slow reply but I didn't see yours until just now; I don't hang out in the Changeling section often and rely on quotes/@s to get signals.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:19:49-07:00","id":1077842,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me these Icon and Glamour Ghosts could be made into Mage Familiars. <br /> <br /> I find the possiblity that you go looking for your Icon only to find out some freaking Mage come along and turned it into a familiar after it took on a life of its own to be very funny.<br /> <br /> There is also the possiblity of Hedge Ghost Claimed.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters with a Hedge Geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:57:51-07:00","id":1077862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077842#post1077842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin Eaters with a Hedge Geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>And new Crossover template is a-go! Ah man, this could be as awesome as the admonitoria! Maybe just make it a character-creation-only style merit for Sin-Eaters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:40:29-07:00","id":1077890,"title":"","content":"Its cool that Icons are still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T20:55:45-07:00","id":1078159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077131#post1077131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge is such a cool place, why do I have to live on Earth <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . All this does is make me screech for Changeling 2E release even more. PLEASE RELEASE IT GOD I'M SO EXCITED <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />!!!!<br /> <br /> I love some of the concepts for Changeling 2E like the Huntsman , God It's going to be so good ^-^ !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If the Fae weren't a bunch of psychotic slave traders, then Arcadia might be a great place to live!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:17:10-07:00","id":1078167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077163#post1077163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... Honestly not sure what I was meant to take away from that. It felt too prosaic; too scattered. I don't have any idea what the Hedge looks like apart from a bit of a psychedelic experience, nor any sense of what it is, why I'd go there... There was more word count spent on the florid examples than on describing what the Hedge actually is.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I didn't like the Hedge being taken in the &quot;PAIN PAIN PAIN ONLY PAIN MY GOODNESS WHY DID YOU EVEN COME HERE PAIN PAIN PAIN&quot; direction, so I'm refreshed to see that something different is taking shape, but I haven't really got any clue from that what that shape actually is.<br /> <br /> What is the Hedge meant to be? What does it look like? What role is it fulfilling? Do I not have to relive my abusive father treating me to the Orwell Special to get some magic fruit anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077179#post1077179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I agree with the assessment that it's exceptionally vague in where the Hedge stands now. I assume we still get hollows and all the fruit and 1ed goodness. Do we still get Dreams connected to the Hedge?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It sounds like the Hedge is constantly changing and adapting itself depending on the individual trying to pass through it. I got the sense that the Hedge will customize itself based on your own subconscious desires, emotions and traumas, which probably means traveling as a group can get extremely chaotic if you aren't focused on the task at hand.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T22:16:25-07:00","id":1078180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1077842#post1077842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me these Icon and Glamour Ghosts could be made into Mage Familiars.<br /> <br /> I find the possiblity that you go looking for your Icon only to find out some freaking Mage come along and turned it into a familiar after it took on a life of its own to be very funny.<br /> <br /> There is also the possiblity of Hedge Ghost Claimed.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters with a Hedge Geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>That they're called &quot;ghosts&quot; does not make them interchangeable with Underworld-resonant ephemeral beings \u2014 this is more likely the Hedge's penchant for turning loose concepts into props and scenery and occasionally actors applied to the place's effect on souls and the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T22:51:24-07:00","id":1078189,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think these things are ghosts in the usual sense, even if they fill the similar thematic niche of being echoes of things lost. These are the passions, the dreams, the ideas of the deceased, but often also of the living. Fairy tale stories are often about echoes of history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T23:57:25-07:00","id":1078198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078189#post1078189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think these things are ghosts in the usual sense, even if they fill the similar thematic niche of being echoes of things lost. These are the passions, the dreams, the ideas of the deceased, but often also of the living. Fairy tale stories are often about echoes of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, the will fly on most of proper ghosts mechanics? I was assuming it was to also broaden Ephemeral Entities in new corebook, with other example being Goblins and Fae there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:25:46-07:00","id":1078369,"title":"","content":"Hedge ghosts use the ephemeral entities rules, yes. Goblins use the same system as Horrors. We've added new powers for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:22:13-07:00","id":1078431,"title":"","content":"Are Hedge Ghost still Ghosts in the Underworld/Death Arcana sense of the word? <br /> <br /> Or are they a different breed of emphereal entities?<br /> <br /> I ask because I'm curious as to what Arcana a Mage would need to use on a Hedge Ghost?<br /> <br /> Do Hedge Ghosts have anchors, do they use essence or glamour, if a human dies in the Hedge could produce both a Hedge Ghost and an Underworld Ghost?<br /> <br /> If Hedge Ghosts are a different breed of Ghost then Underworld Ghost perhaps a new name for them would fit.<br /> <br /> Specters or Phantoms perhaps?<br /> <br /> Can a Changeling create a Hedge Ghost on purpose, like flooding an area of the Hedge with intense emotions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:36:19-07:00","id":1078439,"title":"","content":"Hedge ghosts are a different type of ephemeral entity from the ghosts that you find elsewhere, and they use Glamour rather than Essence.<br /> <br /> Figuring out which Arcana to use to affect a Hedge ghost sounds like a pretty interesting Mystery for a mage to explore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: wow, these smiley faces are a little creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":2229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","user":"Meghan Fitzgerald","date":". 04-14-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:41:24-07:00","id":1078442,"title":"","content":"Does the Hedge have Twilight or would Hedge Ghosts be solid as in the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:15:20-07:00","id":1078461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078439#post1078439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge ghosts are a different type of ephemeral entity from the ghosts that you find elsewhere, and they use Glamour rather than Essence.<br /> <br /> Figuring out which Arcana to use to affect a Hedge ghost sounds like a pretty interesting Mystery for a mage to explore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: wow, these smiley faces are a little creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div> It leaves one wondering if Hedge Ghosts can be made into an exotic Familiar by a Mage. <br /> <br /> If they use Glamour and not essence and the aren't always caused by death, like maybe one is caused by a Changeling falling in love for the first time, or a piece of their soul/icon taking on a life of it's own, I'd say use Fate instead of Death Arcana.<br /> <br /> It does sound like an exciting Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-14-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:17:42-07:00","id":1078495,"title":"","content":"This discussion makes me wonder what other creatures inhabit the Hedge beyond Hedge Ghosts and Goblins (and what is the difference between Goblin and Hobgoblin in Changeling 2e).<br /> <br /> Goblins, Hobgoblins, Changelings, True Fae, Fetches, Huntsmen, are Oniero still a thing?, Cambions?, Hedge Beasts. <br /> <br /> That of course doesn't include the occasional visit by Beast (of the none far sort), Mages, and Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:06:28-07:00","id":1078524,"title":"","content":"One advantage Hedge Ghosts have over Underworld Ghosts is Glamour is alot more available then Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:08:14-07:00","id":1078562,"title":"","content":"Does this mean that Goblins and Hedge Ghosts are now harvesting Glamour the same way Changelings do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:04:40-07:00","id":1078611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078562#post1078562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean that Goblins and Hedge Ghosts are now harvesting Glamour the same way Changelings do?</div> </div> </div> </div> Good question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:47:15-07:00","id":1078670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078439#post1078439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge ghosts are a different type of ephemeral entity from the ghosts that you find elsewhere, and they use Glamour rather than Essence.<br /> <br /> Figuring out which Arcana to use to affect a Hedge ghost sounds like a pretty interesting Mystery for a mage to explore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: wow, these smiley faces are a little creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>HI miss,I'm really enjoying your work so far. May I know,what can hedge ghost do? Do they have special powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T21:01:32-07:00","id":1078746,"title":"","content":"Hedge ghosts harvest Glamour pretty much the same way changelings do, yep. Since goblins use the same system as Horrors, their Dread Powers cost Willpower instead.<br /> <br /> Hedge ghosts can have a variety of Numina, but every Hedge ghost can do a few innate things, like sense Glamour and Goblin Markets, and navigate the Thorns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T21:22:16-07:00","id":1078748,"title":"","content":"Traveling is going to be nicely treacherous, with emotion-baiting ghosts like that. <br /> <br /> Um, one question I wanted to ask is how much relation to the real world there is. First edition was sort of back and forth on that, certain entries implying that the Hedge corresponds roughly to 'parallel' areas in the real world, while others embracing it as an uneven and seemingly random place, I guess stretching more 'perpendicular' to the real world, towards Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2017, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T04:35:38-07:00","id":1078832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078746#post1078746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge ghosts harvest Glamour pretty much the same way changelings do, yep. Since goblins use the same system as Horrors, their Dread Powers cost Willpower instead.<br /> <br /> Hedge ghosts can have a variety of Numina, but every Hedge ghost can do a few innate things, like sense Glamour and Goblin Markets, and navigate the Thorns.</div> </div> </div> </div> I assume changeling a goblin hybrids like Goblin Queens are an exception and still use Glamour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:35:05-07:00","id":1078900,"title":"","content":"I'd hope Goblins have some way of utilizing Glamour, if only so that Changelings can barter with them for it (and vice versa).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:43:52-07:00","id":1078903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078900#post1078900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hope Goblins have some way of utilizing Glamour, if only so that Changelings can barter with them for it (and vice versa).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Goblins just transform Glamour into Willpower? I think it would be easier if rules just state that Goblins change all referance to Willpower for Glamour they have in their pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:01:30-07:00","id":1078907,"title":"","content":"It makes me also wonder if Goblins have a Wyrd score?<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer Goblins to use Glamour then will power, I mean just because they use the horror mechnics doesn't mean they are horrors instead of Fae, they are still Fae, just as using the Ephrmeral rules for Hedge Ghosts, don't make them Underworld Ghosts or Spirits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a dread power that gives them a Wyrd score and the ability to use and harvest Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:09:31-07:00","id":1078912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078746#post1078746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hedge ghosts harvest Glamour pretty much the same way changelings do, yep. Since goblins use the same system as Horrors, their Dread Powers cost Willpower instead.<br /> <br /> Hedge ghosts can have a variety of Numina, but every Hedge ghost can do a few innate things, like sense Glamour and Goblin Markets, and navigate the Thorns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you miss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:27:30-07:00","id":1078921,"title":"","content":"Wait... so Goblins are horrors, but changelings who are turned into goblins use mechanics with no similarities to horror mechanics... that's odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T10:33:17-07:00","id":1078954,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Goblins</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1078921#post1078921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... so Goblins are horrors, but changelings who are turned into goblins use mechanics with no similarities to horror mechanics... that's odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Necessarily.<br /> <br /> &quot;Horrors&quot; by themselves are not a specific creature type (like vampire or werewolf), but a open category of monster that don't fit neatly into an existing gameline. They are intended to allow a storyteller to easily generate antagonists. Its that flexibility that makes it a good choice as the mechanical backing for the diversity of creatures that would be considered Goblins. It is likely they will be using the basic &quot;Horror&quot; framework, with Goblin-specific adjustments (think in the same way ephemeral entities use the same basic rules, but have additional mechanic and traits specific to type).<br /> <br /> I expect Goblins to have a Wyrd score, but will function in mostly the same way as &quot;Potency&quot; does for a standard Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T13:31:59-07:00","id":1079025,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hobgoblin&quot; (or &quot;goblin&quot;) is a term that just means a person or creature that belongs to the Hedge and is infused with its nature, and they can vary wildly. So the Horror rules, which are <b>CofD</b>'s universal mechanism for building supernatural creatures that don't belong to a strict category and are Storyteller characters, are a natural fit here.<br /> <br /> And in the same way that you can build a vampire with the Horror rules that isn't Kindred, you can build a goblin with them that isn't a Goblin Queen of the kind that the Condition creates. There are lots of different potential origins for a goblin--the Condition is just one of them. If a hobgoblin has a specific origin, like being a former changeling or what have you, then you can use those rules instead.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a goblin antagonist can definitely trade in Glamour--after all, the Contracts they sell you use it! The Horror rules allow the Storyteller to create all kinds of unique goblins, and Willpower is the abstraction that system uses to represent whatever a given unique monster might be doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:00:01-07:00","id":1079032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079025#post1079025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hobgoblin&quot; (or &quot;goblin&quot;) is a term that just means a person or creature that belongs to the Hedge and is infused with its nature, and they can vary wildly. So the Horror rules, which are <b>CofD</b>'s universal mechanism for building supernatural creatures that don't belong to a strict category and are Storyteller characters, are a natural fit here.<br /> <br /> And in the same way that you can build a vampire with the Horror rules that isn't Kindred, you can build a goblin with them that isn't a Goblin Queen of the kind that the Condition creates. There are lots of different potential origins for a goblin--the Condition is just one of them. If a hobgoblin has a specific origin, like being a former changeling or what have you, then you can use those rules instead.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a goblin antagonist can definitely trade in Glamour--after all, the Contracts they sell you use it! The Horror rules allow the Storyteller to create all kinds of unique goblins, and Willpower is the abstraction that system uses to represent whatever a given unique monster might be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind telling What aesthetic differences happen when a changeling turns goblin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:25:57-07:00","id":1079044,"title":"","content":"Traditionally goblins can look like anything. Flesh pylons with eyes that surface and dive, tiny pixies, piranha with rat legs, dragons and trees and tree people and bee people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:51:17-07:00","id":1079060,"title":"","content":"I imagine not much changes visually, at first. But give it time; let the Hedge seep into their skin and transform them. If a Changeling's player decides to abandon them and move on, they might get totally and utterly inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:19:56-07:00","id":1079072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079025#post1079025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hobgoblin&quot; (or &quot;goblin&quot;) is a term that just means a person or creature that belongs to the Hedge and is infused with its nature, and they can vary wildly. So the Horror rules, which are <b>CofD</b>'s universal mechanism for building supernatural creatures that don't belong to a strict category and are Storyteller characters, are a natural fit here.<br /> <br /> And in the same way that you can build a vampire with the Horror rules that isn't Kindred, you can build a goblin with them that isn't a Goblin Queen of the kind that the Condition creates. There are lots of different potential origins for a goblin--the Condition is just one of them. If a hobgoblin has a specific origin, like being a former changeling or what have you, then you can use those rules instead.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a goblin antagonist can definitely trade in Glamour--after all, the Contracts they sell you use it! The Horror rules allow the Storyteller to create all kinds of unique goblins, and Willpower is the abstraction that system uses to represent whatever a given unique monster might be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I understand, cool. I assume there will be a Dread Power that interacts with Glamour, like converting it to willpower for the Goblin, and another that grants Goblin Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:38:52-07:00","id":1079087,"title":"","content":"Could probably use the Drain Numen for the first. Dread Powers can access Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:40:12-07:00","id":1079088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079087#post1079087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could probably use the Drain Numen for the first. Dread Powers can access Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div> That could work. Actually Hedge Ghosts would likely have access to the Drain Numen as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:31:34-07:00","id":1079111,"title":"","content":"There could also be something similar to Demon's Aether Eater and Aether Hive Adaptations for cryptids. If there isn't something like that already for goblins, I would imagine that it would be quite simple to create it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:29:57-07:00","id":1079203,"title":"","content":"Mark me down as pleased by the shift away from The Hedge Is Made Out Of Pain (or at least, Anything and Everything that Could Ever Hurt You). The Hedge and its denizens probably constituted my favourite part of 1e, and the spoiler we got a while ago rankled me. I was extremely pleased by the Hedge Denizen/Goblin Queen bits of the other spoiler we got recently as well.<br /> <br /> That being said, I feel like this excerpt is a little too heavy on the &quot;individual stories&quot; side and a little short on &quot;useful information about the hedge for Storytellers and players&quot; side. But maybe that stuff's just elsewhere in the book and this part is just to set tone.","sig