t;things are different&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T14:47:59-07:00","id":1079521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079025#post1079025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hobgoblin&quot; (or &quot;goblin&quot;) is a term that just means a person or creature that belongs to the Hedge and is infused with its nature, and they can vary wildly. So the Horror rules, which are <b>CofD</b>'s universal mechanism for building supernatural creatures that don't belong to a strict category and are Storyteller characters, are a natural fit here.<br /> <br /> And in the same way that you can build a vampire with the Horror rules that isn't Kindred, you can build a goblin with them that isn't a Goblin Queen of the kind that the Condition creates. There are lots of different potential origins for a goblin--the Condition is just one of them. If a hobgoblin has a specific origin, like being a former changeling or what have you, then you can use those rules instead.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a goblin antagonist can definitely trade in Glamour--after all, the Contracts they sell you use it! The Horror rules allow the Storyteller to create all kinds of unique goblins, and Willpower is the abstraction that system uses to represent whatever a given unique monster might be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in the vein of the editions being standalone books, does the changeling core include the basic horror rules and dread powers, for those of us using the god machine core rather than CofD core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:43:36-07:00","id":1079610,"title":"","content":"I wonder which the oneroi (dream goblins) will fall under - horror creation, or ephemeral creation. <br /> <br /> And I kind of wonder if Huntsmen would be made from the new ephemerals? Could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:54:23-07:00","id":1079618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079610#post1079610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder which the oneroi (dream goblins) will fall under - horror creation, or ephemeral creation.<br /> <br /> And I kind of wonder if Huntsmen would be made from the new ephemerals? Could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume they're more or less just ephemeral goblins. Plus, it'd be nice if they fit into onieromachy, and crossed over with mage and beast so that dream goblins can show up to mess with heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:58:14-07:00","id":1079621,"title":"","content":"Its been pretty firmly established that the dreams that pop up in the Hedge are utterly unrelated to the Astral in any way. Unless things have been rather drastically changed, I wouldn't count on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:47:24-07:00","id":1079745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079610#post1079610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder which the oneroi (dream goblins) will fall under - horror creation, or ephemeral creation. <br /> <br /> And I kind of wonder if Huntsmen would be made from the new ephemerals? Could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd guess horror rules, huntsmen are more solid beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T05:13:32-07:00","id":1079751,"title":"","content":"That's assuming they haven't changed along with access to Twilight forms - remember, the Huntsmen came about before we had ephemeral fae. Essence would make a very good replacement for Yearning, for instance, and Bans would just as much restrict a Huntsmen's drives as the story of the hunt did. Well, you can give horrors bans as well, but still. And they have been described as a <i>spirit</i> of the Hunt, after all. Being ephemeral can tie into the whole implecable pursuer, and into the natural you-don't-know-what-form-I-take. <br /> <br /> But we shall see. It could be pretty neat overall, either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T07:50:27-07:00","id":1079791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079751#post1079751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's assuming they haven't changed along with access to Twilight forms - remember, the Huntsmen came about before we had ephemeral fae. Essence would make a very good replacement for Yearning, for instance, and Bans would just as much restrict a Huntsmen's drives as the story of the hunt did. Well, you can give horrors bans as well, but still. And they have been described as a <i>spirit</i> of the Hunt, after all. Being ephemeral can tie into the whole implecable pursuer, and into the natural you-don't-know-what-form-I-take. <br /> <br /> But we shall see. It could be pretty neat overall, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hedge Ghosts use Glamour and if Approaches aren't a thing any more then their is no need for yearning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T10:31:35-07:00","id":1079861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1079791#post1079791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if Approaches aren't a thing any more then their is no need for yearning.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know that for sure. Huntsmen might still use Yearning and just gain it in other ways. Or they might use a completely different resource. We won't know until we see the new version of Huntsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:19:07-07:00","id":1080036,"title":"","content":"Are Trods the same thing as dream roads? Are Trods even still a thing in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T16:13:01-07:00","id":1080055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080036#post1080036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Trods the same thing as dream roads? Are Trods even still a thing in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div> Dream Road lead to peoples dreams, physically, while unless this has changed Trods just lead from Arcadia and Ironside through the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T17:10:56-07:00","id":1080088,"title":"","content":"A lot of ideas are swimming around between this thread and the &quot;David has left&quot; thread, but there is something fundamental that is puzzling me.<br /> <br /> If the Hedge is nothing but pain, why would a changeling ever re-enter it? We know they must, due to the Hollow Merit, as well as Hedge Gate Sense and other currently available Hedge-based Merits. Equally many Goblin Markets take place in the Hedge. If the Hedge automatically inflicts bashing damage simply by entering and staying there, this would appear to undercut any usefulness for the Hedge as a region.<br /> <br /> Then again, I may simply have misread matters. If so, please feel free to correct me. \u263a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T17:25:43-07:00","id":1080092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MhicWombat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080088#post1080088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Hedge is nothing but pain, why would a changeling ever re-enter it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully that was never what the hedge was outside of hyperbole by some fans. It was &quot;Everything in the hedge has the potential to hurt&quot;, that is very different to &quot;Hedge is nothing but pain&quot;. In fact, in real-life everything basically already has the potential for pain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Hedge automatically inflicts bashing damage simply by entering and staying there, this would appear to undercut any usefulness for the Hedge as a region. </div> </div> </div>That's only if you're character decides to walk through thorny undergrowth for long-spans of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:10:59-07:00","id":1080365,"title":"","content":"I'm not going down this road again. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5435_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5435\" data-vbnamecard=\"5435\">MhicWombat</a> - Whatever the Hedge <i>was</i>, re: pain, it's not that anymore. Let's just move forward, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:25:00-07:00","id":1080375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080365#post1080365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going down this road again. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - Whatever the Hedge <i>was</i>, re: pain, it's not that anymore. Let's just move forward, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div> But what is the Hedge now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:39:47-07:00","id":1080383,"title":"","content":"From what I can gather, a thing to emphasize the &quot;beautiful madness&quot; that is Changeling; a place full of fantastical things, hidden places, and lurking dangers. It's a place made of dreams and hopes and bits of the soul left to die, with all that implies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:54:57-07:00","id":1080392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080383#post1080383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can gather, a thing to emphasize the &quot;beautiful madness&quot; that is Changeling; a place full of fantastical things, hidden places, and lurking dangers. It's a place made of dreams and hopes and bits of the soul left to die, with all that implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It honestly sounds like a different perspective on the same place. One just far less pessimistic. In a world as dark as the Chronicles, there must be at least some good and optimistic things in the Hedge made from various beliefs left to die in the hedge such as optimism, faith, faith in justice, cheerfulness, senfse of duty, chariity, you get the idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:21:44-07:00","id":1080483,"title":"","content":"The Hedge is a world, just like ours, with all that implies. It has beauties and grotesqueries and a million things that are both. It's a place influenced by the human mind but not beholden to expectation or belief. It's malleable, because it connects to so many things that can be shaped by living minds -- Arcadia, the Dreaming Roads, even Earth itself. But for all that malleability, it's still just as real when you close your eyes.<br /> <br /> As a whole, the Hedge has no consistent allegiance or moral alignment, any more than Earth does. But when you're rescued by a quixotic goblin knight and his faithful dinosaur steed, or find yourself endlessly turning a mill-wheel that refines human heartbreak into snuff for the Gentry, it certainly can look like it does!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:42:53-07:00","id":1080493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080483#post1080483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge is a world, just like ours, with all that implies. It has beauties and grotesqueries and a million things that are both. It's a place influenced by the human mind but not beholden to expectation or belief. It's malleable, because it connects to so many things that can be shaped by living minds -- Arcadia, the Dreaming Roads, even Earth itself. But for all that malleability, it's still just as real when you close your eyes.<br /> <br /> As a whole, the Hedge has no consistent allegiance or moral alignment, any more than Earth does. But when you're rescued by a quixotic goblin knight and his faithful dinosaur steed, or find yourself endlessly turning a mill-wheel that refines human heartbreak into snuff for the Gentry, it certainly can look like it does!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an awesome image","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:43:58-07:00","id":1080494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080483#post1080483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that refines human heartbreak into snuff for the Gentry...</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the Market rate on that? Or Toxicity?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:51:51-07:00","id":1080538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080383#post1080383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can gather, a thing to emphasize the &quot;beautiful madness&quot; that is Changeling; a place full of fantastical things, hidden places, and lurking dangers. It's a place made of dreams and hopes and bits of the soul left to die, with all that implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>.....there was a point in time when it wasn't this? I would have described the Hedge as this since its inception back in the 1e version of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:55:15-07:00","id":1080540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080494#post1080494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the Market rate on that? Or Toxicity?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A song played on a harp of spider silk, a jar of liquid void, and the last breath of a man dead of heartbreak. Or whatever else the merchant has a need of at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:01:46-07:00","id":1080542,"title":"","content":"My god, imagine the shipping costs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:03:05-07:00","id":1080543,"title":"","content":"Oh, speaking of the snuff mill, any rules on what happens to people kidnapped by Goblins to work in the Hedge? Maybe they become Goblins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T15:58:59-07:00","id":1080605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080538#post1080538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.....there was a point in time when it wasn't this? I would have described the Hedge as this since its inception back in the 1e version of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some folks didn't read David's version of Hedge as this. And, to be fair, David's Changeling was about &quot;beautiful lies and bittersweet truths&quot;, not &quot;beautiful madness&quot;, and his Hedge did emphasize that. It was totally still &quot;a place full of fantastical things, hidden places, and lurking dangers; a place made of dreams and hopes and bits of the soul left to die, with all that implies&quot; though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:31:35-07:00","id":1080628,"title":"","content":"You and I have very different visions of what that means, I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:39:50-07:00","id":1080634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080483#post1080483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a whole, the Hedge has no consistent allegiance or moral alignment, any more than Earth does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue I have with this is that it sort of means I have no idea how to use such a place. If it's just &quot;a place where you can put anything&quot; then it inspires me plot-wise the same level as an empty space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T17:27:35-07:00","id":1080654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080634#post1080634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I have with this is that it sort of means I have no idea how to use such a place. If it's just &amp;quot;a place where you can put anything&amp;quot; then it inspires me plot-wise the same level as an empty space.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Fairy Tale world. Just not only a &quot;Nice&quot; or &quot;Scary&quot; one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T17:49:58-07:00","id":1080662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080654#post1080654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Fairy Tale world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a nice title, but it doesn't actually give any information on what the world is actually like, and what Fairy Tale means is highly subjective.<br /> <br /> For example, goblin knights riding dinosaurs, isn't very &quot;Fairy Tale&quot; in my mind, but it apparently fits the hedge perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:05:40-07:00","id":1080668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080662#post1080662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a nice title, but it doesn't actually give any information on what the world is actually like, and what Fairy Tale means is highly subjective.<br /> <br /> For example, goblin knights riding dinosaurs, isn't very &amp;quot;Fairy Tale&amp;quot; in my mind, but it apparently fits the hedge perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Driven more by narrative and/or whimsy that math and &quot;sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hard to concretely explain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:14:29-07:00","id":1080674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1080668#post1080668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Driven more by narrative and/or whimsy that math and &quot;sense&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hard to concretely explain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what Rose has said it's influenced but not controlled by stories and narratives in the real world. It's worth keeping in mind that that in no way limits things to fairy tales, though even if it did, those stories have pervaded every culture and nook and cranny of our globe and for every one you've heard there's probably a million you haven't. Goblin knights is a pretty good example of that, as both are pretty much straight from fantasy stories and in between invasions and terrorizing cavemen they would probably need something to do to keep busy.<br /> <br /> In this it doesn't seem much different from the old Hedge, which was also supposed to have these things, but examples of which tended to be less bizarre, at least in appearance.<br /> <br /> I'd guess that with the existence of these hedge ghosts, things will be more dangerous. One of the key elements of those 'don't stray from the path' stories was that there was something to tempt or otherwise lure travelers from the path. Visions of lost love, endangered family or friends, treasure or imminent threats. First edition had the danger element of going off the path, but it really didn't add any reason to. The Thorns were bad, thus don't enter the Thorns. Hopefully the ghosts, or something, will offer pitfalls so the Thorns can actually come into play beyond boundaries to 'ring out' opponents.<br /> <br /> Another guess is a big reason to go there is likely to be tied into the players Durances and backstories. You may not know what to do now, but when you're looking at four stories detailing the growth of the player characters you'll probably be able to come up with something suitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-18-2017, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:15:18-07:00","id":1080675,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the helpful and beautiful answers \u263a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T00:51:30-07:00","id":1081347,"title":"","content":"Everyone, even Rose herself, is giving out all these beautiful prose as answers to what the Hedge is... and here I am, completely clueless as to what it is supposed to be. At least the older versions had <i>something</i>, even if some people hated it for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> ... Unless that's exactly the point, and the Hedge is some sort of Wonderland-like world of daydreams? That I can conceptualize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T03:51:45-07:00","id":1081370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081347#post1081347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Unless that's exactly the point, and the Hedge is some sort of Wonderland-like world of daydreams? That I can conceptualize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. The hedge is literally shaped by people's dreams and emotions. So, yes, its literally a daydream made physical. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T08:39:41-07:00","id":1081449,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, Rose's answer was somewhat cryptic, but after thinking about it I think I figured it out.<br /> <br /> In the Hedge Emotion and Story is like the Sun is to Ironic side. After all most things directly or in directly feed on a Glamour, just as the Sun is at the heart of the food chain Ironside.<br /> <br /> So the Hedge is influenced by emotions and story, it shapes the hedge and its cycles just as the Sun shapes weathet cycles, ecosystem, and so on.<br /> <br /> But Iron side is no less real for being shaped by the Sun, the Hedge is no less real for being shaped by Glamour. A simply solar flare doesn't restructure everything Ironside, its has a limit to its mallebity because it does have an objective existance of its own, just as a burst if emotions releasing Glamour doesn't completely rewrite the Hedge.<br /> <br /> So while a hedge plants might bloom when a mortal has an out burst of rage, they don't turn into giant soldier and the blue sky might get stormy when your sad, but the sky doesn't just turn into a feiry inferno every time you get made.<br /> <br /> If you get caught in a pit slick with tears, you can't just will yourself out, or think the pit into meddow, but you might be able make the pit laugh hard enough its tears dry up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:11:59-07:00","id":1081459,"title":"","content":"I want to preface this by saying I <i>do</i> like Rose's Hedge. But I think what some people are struggling with is understanding its narrative role. The Hedge is a fairytale World, yes, but fairytale worlds tend to have intent behind their weirdness. The Labyrinth may look at a casual glance like a place where strange things happen at random for no reason, but everything that happens reinforces the underlying theme of &quot;where anything seems possible and nothing is as it seems&quot;. The labyrinth exists to break Sarah's (and the audience's) expectations - more often than not, expectations it sets up itself. Wonderland seems like a psychedelic trip with no rhyme or reason, but upon closer analysis the vast majority of the apparent nonsense is actually jokes about math and logic. The 10th Kingdom was a very silly mini-series, but as lighthearted and zany as the kingdoms were, their purpose was to deconstruct common fairy tale tropes.<br /> <br /> The point is, fairy tales <i>mean things</i>, and this except of the Hedge writeup does not make it clear what this version of the Hedge is supposed to mean. David's Hedge was about pain, and about how pain, like magic, can be every bit as alluring as it is repellent; every bit as dangerous as it is wonderful. It may have been a little on-the-nose with its metaphor, but I prefer that over being too vague to be recognizable under critical analysis. This Hedge has the superficial trappings of a fairytale world in spades, but it feels shallow because, from this excerpt alone, I can't tell what it's <i>about</i> on a deeper level.<br /> <br /> Of course, knowing Rose's talent at conveying metaphor through mechanics, I am giving her the benefit of the doubt and assuming that this Hedge <i>does</i> mean something, and that meaning will be more clear in the complete text. I'm guessing there's key information in the redacted segment that would help it all come together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-20-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:40:04-07:00","id":1081466,"title":"","content":"I guess the deeper meaning might be that the Hedge is a nexus of sorts between Dreams, Arcadia, and Ironside and so it inherits elements from all their natures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:12:04-07:00","id":1081479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081466#post1081466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the deeper meaning might be that the Hedge is a nexus of sorts between Dreams, Arcadia, and Ironside and so it inherits elements from all their natures.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that it turns the definition of the Hedge into a circular citation:<br /> <br /> &quot;What is <i>the Hedge</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is the world between <i>Earth</i> and <i>Faerie</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What is <i>Faerie</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is the world on the other side of <i>the Hedge</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The other prominent magical neighbor-worlds in ChroD can be summarized by their reflective principles and the nature of their inhabitants \u2014 even the mysterious nature of the Underworld is mitigated by its being a a place where obsessive creatures grasp at life and color dwell and struggle not to fade out while mired in death and rot shut away from the lands of humanity by walls that are thinner around funerary traditions. There's no such unifying feature for goblin things besides a general sense of untrustworthiness and a more personal/immediate version of the reflective nature of the Shadow and the Astral.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine's Infrastructure approaches some of this problem by virtue of its tells explicitly including &quot;weird and out-of-place,&quot; but that's a world-spanning force with a mysterious agenda and a specific practice of using occult confluences to advance its goals, whereas the Wyrd has historically been a little more reactive than that and doesn't have the assumption of an independent plan behind most of what it does in aggregate \u2014 a monster born from someone's nightmares isn't engaged with by changelings as something that the Wyrd created to engage with them, but there needs to be a reason of similar weight and simplicity to &quot;someone reached an emotional tipping point and woke up the spiritual reflection of their kitchen knife&quot; or &quot;the mysterious conspiracy-engine that sits astride the material world found it most efficient to engineer an artificial ghost to keep people out of the study of one of its wealthy pawns.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling's metaphysics have always had an uncomfortable bit of Calvinball occupying the disjunction between &quot;this makes sense in context but looks weird out of it&quot; and &quot;this looks weird and there seems to be no way to acquire the context for it,&quot; and I feel like having an independent working explanation for how and/or why the Hedge operates would do a lot to help with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:20:15-07:00","id":1081485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081466#post1081466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the deeper meaning might be that the Hedge is a nexus of sorts between Dreams, Arcadia, and Ironside and so it inherits elements from all their natures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking for something a bit more Doylist. I understand the Hedge's place in the fictional universe, what I'm not seeing yet is its purpose in the narrative of Changeling: the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:21:08-07:00","id":1081502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081485#post1081485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was looking for something a bit more Doylist. I understand the Hedge's place in the fictional universe, what I'm not seeing yet is its purpose in the narrative of Changeling: the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Changeling </i>is about reclaiming your life. But when you're doing that, you have to take risks and be vulnerable and go places that the people living lives of safety and privilege don't. You can avoid going back to the things that hurt you worst -- Arcadia -- but life is still about risks and climbing out on limbs and admitting that you need things that don't come easy. And then when you do those things, you find that some of them go badly and hurt you, while others are unexpectedly rewarding and growth-encouraging.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is those kinds of necessary risks made into physical reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:27:51-07:00","id":1081506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081502#post1081502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Changeling </i>is about reclaiming your life. But when you're doing that, you have to take risks and be vulnerable and go places that the people living lives of safety and privilege don't. You can avoid going back to the things that hurt you worst -- Arcadia -- but life is still about risks and climbing out on limbs and admitting that you need things that don't come easy. And then when you do those things, you find that some of them go badly and hurt you, while others are unexpectedly rewarding and growth-encouraging.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is those kinds of necessary risks made into physical reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, does this mean there is such a thing as a Goblin Market trip that isn't a... well, let's call it a plot hook? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:31:05-07:00","id":1081509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081506#post1081506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, does this mean there is such a thing as a Goblin Market trip that isn't a... well, let's call it a plot hook? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:40:09-07:00","id":1081510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081509#post1081509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, a Goblin Market trip that ends with you actually getting what you want without getting ripped off and it's not just because its your first trip and they want you to come back. If the Hedge is it's own self-sufficient world, it should be possible. Anyway, I was just making a joke, where plot hook = &quot;life sucks for you, sonny jim!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:46:50-07:00","id":1081512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081510#post1081510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, a Goblin Market trip that ends with you actually getting what you want without getting ripped off and it's not just because its your first trip and they want you to come back. If the Hedge is it's own self-sufficient world, it should be possible. Anyway, I was just making a joke, where plot hook = &quot;life sucks for you, sonny jim!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Goblin Markets are dangerous, but visits to them are not always disasters! And goblins, while their motivations and ethics frequently conflict with changelings', are not the drug dealers from an 80s edutainment special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:05:44-07:00","id":1081525,"title":"","content":"So, there can be such things as truly heroic, or at least a bit morally above average Goblins? Always been wondering about that, cause I wanted a Hedgebeast Companion that I could really be friends with","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T13:13:20-07:00","id":1081555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081502#post1081502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Changeling </i>is about reclaiming your life. But when you're doing that, you have to take risks and be vulnerable and go places that the people living lives of safety and privilege don't. You can avoid going back to the things that hurt you worst -- Arcadia -- but life is still about risks and climbing out on limbs and admitting that you need things that don't come easy. And then when you do those things, you find that some of them go badly and hurt you, while others are unexpectedly rewarding and growth-encouraging.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is those kinds of necessary risks made into physical reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I'm glad to see it is intended to have a strong narrative role. I'll be interested to see how that is reflected in the omitted section(s) and mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T18:36:08-07:00","id":1081654,"title":"","content":"Wonderland is what I pictured from the new text. The earlier text seemed darker to me. I have no particular preference, but I have a much harder time explaining how to describe the earlier expression to someone that doesn't get it on their own. If someone says to me &quot;you say the Hedge is like Wonderland but which version?&quot; then I would say all of them, sometimes all at once, savvy? There is advantage in that and the other way had its advantages as well. There is risk to really hone into a narrow laser-like focus. Pros and cons either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T18:48:54-07:00","id":1081657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081654#post1081654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonderland is what I pictured from the new text. The earlier text seemed darker to me. I have no particular preference, but I have a much harder time explaining how to describe the earlier expression to someone that doesn't get it on their own. If someone says to me &quot;you say the Hedge is like Wonderland but which version?&quot; then I would say all of them, sometimes all at once, savvy? There is advantage in that and the other way had its advantages as well. There is risk to really hone into a narrow laser-like focus. Pros and cons either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're describing its superficial qualities, not its narrative role. I'm not asking what fictional fairy tale world it resembles, I'm asking what it does to enhance the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T20:37:43-07:00","id":1081682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081502#post1081502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Changeling </i>is about reclaiming your life. But when you're doing that, you have to take risks and be vulnerable and go places that the people living lives of safety and privilege don't. You can avoid going back to the things that hurt you worst -- Arcadia -- but life is still about risks and climbing out on limbs and admitting that you need things that don't come easy. And then when you do those things, you find that some of them go badly and hurt you, while others are unexpectedly rewarding and growth-encouraging.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is those kinds of necessary risks made into physical reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the context of Pain from the previous version is still here. Except that it's been widened and softened to Risk.<br /> <br /> Now I finally get it. Risk. It all clicks in.<br /> <br /> Ironside is Reality, and Faerie is Fantasy. The Hedge is what separates Ironside from Faerie. Risk is what separates Reality from Fantasy. The Hedge is what connects Ironside and Faerie. Risk is what connects Reality and Fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T20:41:36-07:00","id":1081683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081502#post1081502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Changeling </i>is about reclaiming your life. But when you're doing that, you have to take risks and be vulnerable and go places that the people living lives of safety and privilege don't. You can avoid going back to the things that hurt you worst -- Arcadia -- but life is still about risks and climbing out on limbs and admitting that you need things that don't come easy. And then when you do those things, you find that some of them go badly and hurt you, while others are unexpectedly rewarding and growth-encouraging.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is those kinds of necessary risks made into physical reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a word, &quot;adventure&quot;. Both in the traditional and non-traditional senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T20:48:06-07:00","id":1081687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081682#post1081682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the context of Pain from the previous version is still here. Except that it's been widened and softened to Risk.<br /> <br /> Now I finally get it. Risk. It all clicks in.<br /> <br /> Ironside is Reality, and Faerie is Fantasy. The Hedge is what separates Ironside from Faerie. Risk is what separates Reality from Fantasy. The Hedge is what connects Ironside and Faerie. Risk is what connects Reality and Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also feeds nicely into the loose economic theme that Changeling metaphysics approach* through the lens of Fortune \u2014 almost every move you can make constitutes some form of investment, and losses stemming from losing out on a risky venture can be very painful indeed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Even without Goblin Markets and Goldspinners and the like, I will never get tired of pointing out that Changeling was the first line in Chronicles to have a literal and explicit mercenary bloc as <i>corebook antagonists</i>.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T21:03:09-07:00","id":1081692,"title":"","content":"Risk, Bargains, and Adventures.<br /> <br /> Already I'm liking Changeling more than I did a few days ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T21:42:19-07:00","id":1081705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081682#post1081682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the context of Pain from the previous version is still here. Except that it's been widened and softened to Risk.<br /> <br /> Now I finally get it. Risk. It all clicks in.<br /> <br /> Ironside is Reality, and Faerie is Fantasy. The Hedge is what separates Ironside from Faerie. Risk is what separates Reality from Fantasy. The Hedge is what connects Ironside and Faerie. Risk is what connects Reality and Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I like that. I do hope that will be conveyed a bit more clearly in the full text, but this is a really cool interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T22:42:10-07:00","id":1081715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081657#post1081657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're describing its superficial qualities, not its narrative role. I'm not asking what fictional fairy tale world it resembles, I'm asking what it does to enhance the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not trying to answer your question. I'm not sure enough information was provided to know the answer, but good luck with that. I was trying to make a statement of what the text conveyed to me. I don't think answering &quot;what&quot; is superficial and &quot;why&quot; more deep. I need both answers. Sorry, can't help with your quest. I assume the book will at least answer your question. It should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:44:47-07:00","id":1081790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081485#post1081485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was looking for something a bit more Doylist. I understand the Hedge's place in the fictional universe, what I'm not seeing yet is its purpose in the narrative of Changeling: the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had to look up Doylist. I tend to be a mix if Watsonian and Doylist leaning heavily towards Watsonian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:48:15-07:00","id":1081791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081682#post1081682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the context of Pain from the previous version is still here. Except that it's been widened and softened to Risk.<br /> <br /> Now I finally get it. Risk. It all clicks in.<br /> <br /> Ironside is Reality, and Faerie is Fantasy. The Hedge is what separates Ironside from Faerie. Risk is what separates Reality from Fantasy. The Hedge is what connects Ironside and Faerie. Risk is what connects Reality and Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good summary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:42:41-07:00","id":1081833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081790#post1081790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had to look up Doylist. I tend to be a mix if Watsonian and Doylist leaning heavily towards Watsonian.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really something you <i>are</i>, it's a quality of commentary on fiction. When you explain something in fiction from an in-universe perspective, the explanation is wattsonian. When you explain it from an out of universe perspective, the explanation is Doylist. Both are important for critical analysis of fictional works.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for a concrete example, a Wattsonian explanation of the purpose of the eponymous Labyrinth in Jim Henson's film would be that it's there to prevent Sarah from getting to Toby (or in the graphic novels, to test the ice queen's love for Jareth.) A Doylist explanation would be that the Labyrinth exists to set up and then break audience expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-21-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:36:09-07:00","id":1082070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081705#post1081705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I like that. I do hope that will be conveyed a bit more clearly in the full text, but this is a really cool interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still worry about that, since the only bit missing from the preview appears to be the dreaming roads (which appear to have replaced bastions).<br /> <br /> I hope it'll be more obvious in the mechanics section I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:41:40-07:00","id":1082072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1081833#post1081833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not really something you <i>are</i>, it's a quality of commentary on fiction. When you explain something in fiction from an in-universe perspective, the explanation is wattsonian. When you explain it from an out of universe perspective, the explanation is Doylist. Both are important for critical analysis of fictional works.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for a concrete example, a Wattsonian explanation of the purpose of the eponymous Labyrinth in Jim Henson's film would be that it's there to prevent Sarah from getting to Toby (or in the graphic novels, to test the ice queen's love for Jareth.) A Doylist explanation would be that the Labyrinth exists to set up and then break audience expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was referring to personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:53:13-07:00","id":1082075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1082070#post1082070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still worry about that, since the only bit missing from the preview appears to be the dreaming roads (which appear to have replaced bastions).<br /> <br /> I hope it'll be more obvious in the mechanics section I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I share your worry, but I am comforted by Rose's track record of expressing metaphor through mechanics. Requiem 2e is a shining example of this done well, so I trust she will be able to pull it off with Changeling too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T22:18:25-07:00","id":1082153,"title":"","content":"Seriously. Constant mantras of fear in these forums. 'Those things I don't know about are probably going to be a disappointment.'<br /> <br /> It's coming, and there's no need to be superstitious. Thinking something might turn out well is not going to fate it to awfulness. There's more open development that will be revealed, I'm sure, and Rose is a proven developer and writer. Blood and Smoke was fantastic. And it sounds like her team aren't a bunch of slack-jawed yokels who've never played a game before. And they're all fans of Changeling. Even if there are aspects you don't like, there's like two other builds that are going to be available you can hack off of and this forum is full of homebrewers and the system has proven itself very easy to move around like that, especially regarding setting changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  No offense intended to slack-jawed yokels. 04-22-2017, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:07:51-07:00","id":1082246,"title":"","content":"I kinda hope we get some magical weather Tilts. I'd like a bit more in the way of weather magic in 2e. Felt kinda weird that Elementals couldn't conjure a rainstorm unless they joined the Spring Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T08:41:55-07:00","id":1082277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1082246#post1082246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Felt kinda weird that Elementals couldn't conjure a rainstorm unless they joined the Spring Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Make rainfall&quot; was called out as within the ability of Calling the Elements and there was a generalized &quot;make any non-extreme weather within spec for the local climate&quot; clause in the Contracts of the Wild, both of which were affinity purchases for Elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T10:47:58-07:00","id":1082311,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Calling the Elements only let you call/direct the element as it existed, didn't it? I'll have to double-check Wilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T17:50:33-07:00","id":1082456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1082153#post1082153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously. Constant mantras of fear in these forums. 'Those things I don't know about are probably going to be a disappointment.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's the opposite. We are hopeful about the rest of the content, we are worried about the bits we've seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:32:49-07:00","id":1082790,"title":"","content":"I've kind of been prodding at a 1.5e conversion for Changeling in my head today, amid preparing for a trip, and an idea occurred to me on how to make the Hedge a place you'd want to go.<br /> <br /> In 1e, Talespinning was one of my favourite mechanics. It was a really neat ability that was the Changeling equivalent of &quot;Yes, And&quot; in improv; it let you adjust the scene in such a way that didn't end the story. The best feature of it was that it never took away what you got for your action. If you used the Talespinning to get money, you <i>got</i> money; the drawback never instantly took it from you. It was never a perfect system, but it was a really good one.<br /> <br /> In this conversion I've been monkeying with, the idea occurred to me that Talespinning would, and should, be really corrosive towards Clarity. After all, here is the universe operating by rhyme and unreason; you can't deny it or pretend it isn't because you're the one causing it. It feels like using Talespinning should be cause for an instant Clarity breaking point.<br /> <br /> The Hedge, though, does operate by rhyme and unreason; it's a place where a bag of dead spiders is worth a fistful of goblin gold; where magic fruit can heal wounds. It'd make sense to make it far more relaxed there. Rather than risking a Clarity breaking point, Talespinning could be far easier in the Hedge, and have far more diverse possible ends. It'd make the Hedge exceptionally alluring, while also making it dangerous, because the opportunity is there; it can give you what you want and you <i>will</i> get it. You just... Might get something else too.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this would work with 2e - it wasn't my intention in writing this post to make this a suggestion for 2e - but I think it works well with that too. The Hedge becomes the stage for an adventure; where necessary risks for your chosen reward are just waiting for you to pull the right thread.<br /> <br /> Just a thought I felt was neat. It also means Goblin Markets still serve a purpose; you can get what you want without having to take (the same kind of) risks, as long as you can pay the price.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:34:15-07:00","id":1084423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1082790#post1082790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also means Goblin Markets still serve a purpose; you can get what you want without having to take (the same kind of) risks, as long as you can pay the price.</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm... what? Since when do Goblin Markets not serve a purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-27-2017, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:03:13-07:00","id":1084440,"title":"","content":"There's a misunderstanding. Including a feature in the Hedge that lets you just find whatever you want, carte blanche, would obviate a lot of the purpose of Goblin Markets. Talespinning - with its inclusion of a consequence for your choice to cheat the system - has a built-in feature to ensure it <i>doesn't</i> obviate Goblin Markets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:51:45-07:00","id":1084461,"title":"","content":"EDIT - Oh, I think Goblin Markets offer a lot more than just tokens and goblin fruit that you can't just stumble on. I think its safe to say that your way won't impact the Goblin Markets in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-27-2017, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:42:22-07:00","id":1084477,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is the point; it isn't meant to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T01:21:46-07:00","id":1085734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077119-a-walk-in-the-hedge?p=1084477#post1084477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is the point; it isn't meant to.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:24:31-07:00","id":1087978,"title":"","content":"The point is that Goblin Markets won't lose their niche, just because of this added feature.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the delayed reply, but I am presently in the Savegre cloud forest. Internet is hard to come by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":